---
import PlaygroundDemo from "../playground/PlaygroundDemo.astro";
import Code from "#/ui/core/Code.astro";
import Tabs from "#/ui/core/Tabs.astro";
import LogotypeLight from "#/assets/logotype-light.svg";
import LogotypeDark from "#/assets/logotype-dark.svg";
import Icon from "../core/Icon/Icon.astro";
---

<div class="grow pd-x-layout flex flex-col">
  <div class="flex flex-col items-center py-15 gap-6">
    <header class="layout-container text-center flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h1 class="heading text-4xl font-display leading-snug">
        <LogotypeLight class="logotype block dark:hidden" />
        <LogotypeDark class="logotype hidden dark:block" />
        <span class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 font-medium">
          Programming Language
        </span>
      </h1>

      <p
        class="font-display text-xl text-balance text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 leading-relaxed"
      >
        A programming language that transpiles to idiomatic
        TypeScript/Rust/Python types, allowing effortless type-safe interop
        between languages.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="max-w-xl w-full flex justify-center">
      <Tabs
        items={[
          { id: "install-xnix", label: "Linux/macOS" },
          { id: "install-windows", label: "Windows" },
        ]}
        active="install-xnix"
        style="code"
      >
        <Fragment slot="install-xnix">
          <Code
            code="curl -fsSL https://genotype-lang.org/install.sh | sh"
            lang="bash"
            copy
          />
        </Fragment>

        <Fragment slot="install-windows">
          <Code
            code="irm https://genotype-lang.org/install.ps1 | iex"
            lang="powershell"
            copy
          />
        </Fragment>
      </Tabs>
    </div>

    <div class="flex gap-4 justify-center">
      <a href="/docs/getting-started" class="button button-main is-get-started">
        Get Started
      </a>

      <a href="/playground" class="button is-playground"> Playground </a>
    </div>

    <div class="links flex gap-4 justify-center">
      <a href="https://github.com/kossnocorp/genotype">
        <Icon id="github" style="brands" />
        GitHub
      </a>

      <text-del></text-del>

      <a href="https://github.com/kossnocorp/genotype/discussions">
        <Icon id="forum" style="300" />
        Discussions
      </a>

      <text-del></text-del>

      <a href="https://discord.gg/vXCfjVbj9J">
        <Icon id="discord" style="brands" />
        Discord
      </a>
    </div>

    <div
      class="layout-container flex h-200 min-h-0 flex-col overflow-hidden border border-transparent dark:border-gray-800"
    >
      <PlaygroundDemo lineNumbers={false} />
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="prose dark:prose-invert mx-auto w-full pb-15">
    <h2>Why Genotype?</h2>

    <p>
      Genotype is built for teams working with multiple programming languages
      (e.g., TypeScript front-end with Rust back-end), building API clients,
      file formats and standards, gradual language migration, etc.
    </p>

    <p>
      Genotype is a small language that you can learn in 15 minutes, but it is
      feature-rich and allows expressing the most complex data structures. It
      has generics, supports recursive data types, and allows target-specific
      fine-tuning via annotations.
    </p>

    <p>
      It isn't opinionated and adapts to the ecosystem instead of creating one.
      Want to generate Zod or Effect schemas instead of plain types? No problem! Need a
      ready-to-ship package or want to generate code right into existing
      modules? Can do! Need support for legacy Python versions? Absolutely.
    </p>

    <p>
      Unlike most machine-generated code, the code Genotype produces is clean,
      follows the idiomatic naming for types and files, and follows the common
      conventions.
    </p>

    <p>
      And of course, Genotype is AI agent-ready and provides <a
        href="/docs/toolchain/skill/">skill</a
      >, <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a>, and leaves code comment breadcrumbs
      to help steer LLMs into using it correctly.
    </p>

    <h3>Why Not Protobuf or Similar?</h3>

    <p>
      Genotype indeed overlaps with Protocol Buffers, but it doesn't impose the
      transport or storage format. It focuses on producing clean idiomatic types
      with minimal to no runtime instead of optimizing data transfer
      performance. TypeScript has no runtime at all. Rust and Python use
      standard Serde and Pydantic to close the gaps.
    </p>

    <p>
      As a result, it better fits when developing API clients and web app
      client-server interop. It's more flexible and allows more complex data
      types and data shapes Protobuf cannot express directly.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section
    class="mx-auto w-full max-w-2xl px-1 md:px-4 pb-12 md:pb-21 flex justify-between items-center gap-4"
  >
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
      <h3>Interested?</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-500">
        No lock-in and trivial to migrate from.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
      <a href="/docs/getting-started" class="button button-main is-get-started">
        Get Started
      </a>

      <a href="/playground" class="button is-playground"> Playground </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer
    class="links layout-container flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 border-t border-(--color-divider) py-6 text-sm text-(--color-link-secondary)"
  >
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
      <span>Sasha Koss © 2026</span>
      <text-del></text-del>
      <a href="https://koss.nocorp.me/mit">MIT License</a>
    </div>

    <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
      <a href="https://github.com/kossnocorp/genotype" aria-label="GitHub">
        <Icon id="github" style="brands" class="icon-md" />
      </a>

      <a href="https://discord.gg/vXCfjVbj9J" aria-label="Discord">
        <Icon id="discord" style="brands" class="icon-md" />
      </a>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <style>
    @reference "#/styles/global.css";

    .heading {
      @apply font-sans;
      --font-display--font-variation-settings: "wdth" 32;
    }

    .logotype {
      @apply mx-auto;
      height: 4rem;
    }

    .button.is-get-started {
      @apply text-base px-4;
    }

    .button.is-playground {
      @apply px-4 border border-gray-500 dark:border-(--color-divider) bg-transparent;

      --button-text-base: var(--color-gray-600);
      @variant dark {
        --button-text-base: var(--color-gray-200);
      }
    }

    .links {
      @apply flex items-center gap-3 dark:text-gray-600;

      & a {
        @apply decoration-0 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-ms text-(--color-link-secondary) hover:text-(--color-link-secondary-hover);
      }
    }
  </style>
</div>
